Why is that a thing?

48
00:03:45,480 --> 00:03:46,140
So weird.

49
00:03:49,460 --> 00:03:50,140
Oh, yeah.

50
00:03:50,720 --> 00:03:51,040
Okay.

51
00:03:52,100 --> 00:03:54,160
Look at that silly burp down there.

52
00:03:55,060 --> 00:03:56,940
That is the weirdest burp I've ever seen.

53
00:03:58,220 --> 00:04:01,640
In fact, I never really paid attention to these screens in the back here.

54
00:04:01,940 --> 00:04:03,680
Let's see if we can see something in this.

55
00:04:05,260 --> 00:04:05,700
Sunset.

56
00:04:06,500 --> 00:04:06,940
Clouds.

57
00:04:07,140 --> 00:04:08,460
Why is this so low res?

58
00:04:10,460 --> 00:04:13,680
Like, if you have a background like this, why wouldn't you turn up the settings at least?

59
00:04:15,860 --> 00:04:16,300
Uh...

60
00:04:16,380 --> 00:04:18,900
Cacti with little flowers on top.

61
00:04:19,020 --> 00:04:19,880
What the hell is that about?

62
00:04:21,340 --> 00:04:24,100
I ain't seen no cacti with flowers growing on them.

63
00:04:27,160 --> 00:04:28,440
And these are what?

64
00:04:29,380 --> 00:04:30,600
Dried out cacti?

65
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:34,320
Sand cacti.

66
00:04:34,560 --> 00:04:35,460
Or whatever that is.

67
00:04:37,080 --> 00:04:37,620
Interesting.

68
00:04:41,180 --> 00:04:41,620
Okay.

69
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:43,160
Guys, whoa!

70
00:04:43,720 --> 00:04:45,520
I just got a shake in my hands.

71
00:04:46,460 --> 00:04:47,500
A milkshake.

72
00:04:47,540 --> 00:04:48,000
It just appeared.

73
00:04:48,200 --> 00:04:49,080
It's in my left hand.

74
00:04:49,180 --> 00:04:49,720
What the hell?

75
00:04:50,760 --> 00:04:51,420
Throw it away.

76
00:04:53,160 --> 00:04:53,960
I'm going in.

77
00:04:57,220 --> 00:04:58,480
11th was the last time.

78
00:04:58,600 --> 00:04:59,620
That's a while ago, man.

79
00:05:01,440 --> 00:05:02,560
Fucking hell, I've been busy.

80
00:05:06,350 --> 00:05:07,410
What was I doing?

81
00:05:09,410 --> 00:05:11,310
Oh, guys, guys.

82
00:05:12,530 --> 00:05:15,850
The orphan crusher was working beautifully.

83
00:05:17,090 --> 00:05:19,370
Last time, remember how much I found?

84
00:05:19,950 --> 00:05:21,230
It was wild.

85
00:05:22,010 --> 00:05:26,170
Such a good... I didn't even think about... Guys, I spawned in.

86
00:05:26,910 --> 00:05:29,110
I did not control my hands just now.

87
00:05:29,370 --> 00:05:30,610
It happened automatically.

88
00:05:30,990 --> 00:05:33,910
I saw this, immediately went up.

89
00:05:34,510 --> 00:05:35,850
And started mining.

90
00:05:36,050 --> 00:05:37,130
I didn't even question it.

91
00:05:37,430 --> 00:05:38,530
It was all automatic.

92
00:05:39,690 --> 00:05:41,510
I think Minecraft is in my blood now.

93
00:05:42,870 --> 00:05:44,290
I don't know how else to say it.

94
00:05:46,490 --> 00:05:49,290
Other than that, what did I do last time?

95
00:05:49,350 --> 00:05:51,630
Oh yeah, I got three elytra, by the way.

96
00:05:52,010 --> 00:05:54,330
Nothing fancy, you know, just everyday things.

97
00:05:55,110 --> 00:05:59,490
Going to the end and casually just getting all the most amazing loot.

98
00:06:00,270 --> 00:06:02,230
Without dying, I might add.

99
00:06:03,600 --> 00:06:05,680
Quite the expedition that was.

100
00:06:07,380 --> 00:06:10,240
I think last stream was actually only filled with W's.

101
00:06:11,200 --> 00:06:12,900
We didn't have any L's at all.

102
00:06:13,960 --> 00:06:15,300
Throughout the entire thing.

103
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:18,160
It's a rare thing to happen, but it did happen.

104
00:06:19,480 --> 00:06:20,000
Yeah.

105
00:06:20,780 --> 00:06:22,200
What was I doing down here?

106
00:06:25,760 --> 00:06:27,100
I found a music disc.

107
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:27,760
Chirp.

108
00:06:30,870 --> 00:06:31,890
Wait, why did I come down here?

109
00:06:35,460 --> 00:06:37,140
Did I just light up areas?

110
00:06:37,420 --> 00:06:38,160
Is that what I was doing?

111
00:06:38,880 --> 00:06:40,140
Oh, no, no, no, no, no.

112
00:06:40,260 --> 00:06:40,980
I remember now.

113
00:06:41,240 --> 00:06:43,260
I came down here to find the dude.

114
00:06:43,940 --> 00:06:45,300
I know about a guy, right?

115
00:06:45,440 --> 00:06:46,600
I know a guy who knows a guy.

116
00:06:46,780 --> 00:06:47,260
That's right.

117
00:06:48,340 --> 00:06:50,580
But I do know that he's not here.

118
00:06:50,960 --> 00:06:53,560
I know where to find him, but I need to go to the other entrance.

119
00:06:55,100 --> 00:06:59,460
There's another cave entrance to the north of the community center.

120
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:04,420
You know what, we're just gonna keep calling it the community center as well.

121
00:07:04,940 --> 00:07:05,820
It has many names.

122
00:07:06,640 --> 00:07:07,580
Oh, where am I right now?

123
00:07:09,320 --> 00:07:10,860
I need a map stat.

124
00:07:13,040 --> 00:07:15,300
I gotta be able to see if I'm close to home.

125
00:07:16,260 --> 00:07:19,100
Otherwise, what I'm doing right here may be fruitless.

126
00:07:22,240 --> 00:07:24,220
But you know what, I see darkness, I light it up.

127
00:07:24,340 --> 00:07:24,640
What do you want?

128
00:07:26,360 --> 00:07:27,440
It has to happen.

129
00:07:30,340 --> 00:07:31,400
Level 30!

130
00:07:33,680 --> 00:07:35,760
We can finally enchant shit again.

131
00:07:36,220 --> 00:07:42,540
I may, honestly, save my levels until 33 and spend it all on that pickaxe.

132
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:44,280
That requires 33 levels.

133
00:07:45,540 --> 00:07:46,820
It is just that good.

134
00:07:47,080 --> 00:07:48,040
I may do it.

135
00:07:49,900 --> 00:07:52,100
I think it's worth it to get a good pickaxe again.

136
00:07:52,300 --> 00:07:52,920
Because look at this.

137
00:07:53,620 --> 00:07:54,640
What is that even?

138
00:07:57,520 --> 00:07:58,380
It's nothing.

139
00:08:02,920 --> 00:08:04,300
Gotta get back on top, right?

140
00:08:06,400 --> 00:08:10,520
I do remember coal was lacking severely, so we gotta get our hands on that.

141
00:08:10,640 --> 00:08:12,160
Our grubby hands all over it.

142
00:08:12,920 --> 00:08:13,860
Fondle that coal.

143
00:08:20,380 --> 00:08:21,060
Oh, yeah.

144
00:08:21,560 --> 00:08:22,420
There's actually quite a lot.

145
00:08:25,660 --> 00:08:26,980
Why is there so much coal here?

146
00:08:27,820 --> 00:08:28,520
Look at this!

147
00:08:32,440 --> 00:08:33,680
This has to be the end.

148
00:08:38,660 --> 00:08:39,840
It keeps going.

149
00:08:43,940 --> 00:08:45,940
Wow, that was a hole.

150
00:08:46,200 --> 00:08:47,340
And there's more up here too.

151
00:08:48,840 --> 00:08:50,440
Getting experience as well.

152
00:08:51,900 --> 00:08:54,440
You truly can't go wrong, mining coal.

153
00:08:58,180 --> 00:09:00,400
Man, I feel so light on my feet.

154
00:09:01,060 --> 00:09:03,860
I mean, in real life, but also in the game.

155
00:09:04,680 --> 00:09:06,920
And it's not because of the elight-ra.

156
00:09:07,400 --> 00:09:08,420
That's a horrible pun.

157
00:09:09,540 --> 00:09:13,860
It's just that getting so much stuff last time is like, ah, nice.

158
00:09:14,080 --> 00:09:20,520
I no longer have this massive weight bearing down on me mentally of, like, losing things, you know?

159
00:09:21,900 --> 00:09:23,520
In fact, I'm a winner now.

160
00:09:24,860 --> 00:09:26,200
I have to remember this today.

161
00:09:26,940 --> 00:09:27,860
Today I'm a winner.

162
00:09:30,020 --> 00:09:31,820
And we won't be taking any else.

163
00:09:33,280 --> 00:09:34,540
I love that expression.

164
00:09:34,920 --> 00:09:39,360
I've adopted it ever since I heard other people say it online and now it's like become a thing I say.

165
00:09:42,320 --> 00:09:44,760
I'm gonna go down here and light this up as well.

166
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:47,780
I'm having a good time just lighting things up and finding ores.

167
00:09:51,680 --> 00:09:52,660
Join here.

168
00:09:55,060 --> 00:10:00,660
Do that... Minecraft is a pretty good game, guys.

169
00:10:01,300 --> 00:10:02,100
What can I say?

170
00:10:04,740 --> 00:10:07,880
The crazy thing is, I think the more I play it, the more I like it.

171
00:10:11,280 --> 00:10:14,740
Because I remember how I felt about the game when I played it in the first season, right?

172
00:10:14,860 --> 00:10:15,960
Like, it was fun, of course.

173
00:10:16,660 --> 00:10:19,260
But I feel like I like it more now than I did back then.

174
00:10:20,940 --> 00:10:21,740
Even more so.

175
00:10:22,300 --> 00:10:23,200
How do you explain that?

176
00:10:24,820 --> 00:10:26,080
So we have green over there.

177
00:10:26,560 --> 00:10:29,600
The fact that I lit all of this has to mean that I'm close to home.

178
00:10:30,740 --> 00:10:32,340
Otherwise, why would I do it, right?

179
00:10:36,020 --> 00:10:36,380
Yeah.

180
00:10:36,800 --> 00:10:38,180
Oh, that's a bit too dark, I think.

181
00:10:41,560 --> 00:10:42,080
Yeah.

182
00:10:42,980 --> 00:10:44,020
That looks good.

183
00:10:44,380 --> 00:10:46,900
This looks a little too dark over there in the corner.

184
00:10:48,820 --> 00:10:49,480
Oh, yeah.

185
00:10:50,260 --> 00:10:51,220
That is a problem.

186
00:10:56,460 --> 00:10:57,180
And there.

187
00:10:58,520 --> 00:10:59,440
How many torches?

188
00:10:59,700 --> 00:11:00,240
I have enough.

189
00:11:00,520 --> 00:11:03,420
And I found a bunch of coal, so we're actually chilling right now.

190
00:11:06,600 --> 00:11:08,040
Haven't seen any enemies, really.

191
00:11:08,280 --> 00:11:09,320
So that's good news.

192
00:11:13,040 --> 00:11:14,800
I think I may just dig straight up now.

193
00:11:15,340 --> 00:11:19,320
Just to see where I am in the world and, you know, take stock of the situation.

194
00:11:20,900 --> 00:11:22,600
Fix my inventory, all that.

195
00:11:22,800 --> 00:11:23,900
Say hi to all the villagers.

196
00:11:24,880 --> 00:11:30,780
And of course, look in amazement at the wonderful house I made last time.

197
00:11:34,640 --> 00:11:35,680
It is indeed wonderful.

198
00:11:35,860 --> 00:11:36,760
How do I... Oh.

199
00:11:38,920 --> 00:11:39,640
There we go.

200
00:11:41,160 --> 00:11:42,480
I'll take all this coal as well.

201
00:11:44,040 --> 00:11:45,060
Think about it like this.

202
00:11:45,200 --> 00:11:49,380
Every time I pick up this coal here, obviously I get experience immediately for mining it.

203
00:11:50,280 --> 00:11:55,440
But that coal will also turn all the stone I have at home into even more experience.

204
00:11:56,520 --> 00:11:58,240
So it's like a double dip.

205
00:11:59,960 --> 00:12:01,720
I get so much out of mining this.

206
00:12:08,680 --> 00:12:11,620
But of course, I need a better pickaxe.

207
00:12:19,140 --> 00:12:22,420
33, here I come, and then I'm actually gonna fix that pickaxe.

208
00:12:27,930 --> 00:12:31,670
Or... I try to make a netherite pickaxe.

209
00:12:33,450 --> 00:12:34,770
I made... Yeah, actually.

210
00:12:34,950 --> 00:12:36,830
Oh, but we need the diamond first.

211
00:12:37,350 --> 00:12:39,430
We gotta turn the diamond into netherite.

212
00:12:40,810 --> 00:12:41,670
Yeah, okay.

213
00:12:41,770 --> 00:12:43,070
We need to do the diamond first, actually.

214
00:12:43,430 --> 00:12:44,850
I forgot about that just now.

215
00:12:47,030 --> 00:12:47,830
But that's fine.

216
00:12:52,540 --> 00:12:53,680
Let's get one here as well.

217
00:12:53,980 --> 00:12:54,600
Just like that.

218
00:12:56,740 --> 00:12:58,940
So, wait, what happened here?

219
00:13:00,400 --> 00:13:02,100
Oh, I remember this spot now.

220
00:13:02,300 --> 00:13:03,400
I went up there, didn't I?

221
00:13:04,740 --> 00:13:06,000
That is a bit too dark, I think.

222
00:13:06,060 --> 00:13:07,260
I think enemies can spawn up there.

223
00:13:10,940 --> 00:13:19,200
If enemies can spawn in a tight little cubicle, like right under my village, if you remember, then they can most surely spawn up here too.

224
00:13:22,310 --> 00:13:24,190
On, like, a singular block, you know?

225
00:13:25,650 --> 00:13:26,330
There we go.

226
00:13:30,390 --> 00:13:35,490
There is one good thing about this pickaxe that I have right now, and it's the fact that it doesn't have mending.

227
00:13:35,970 --> 00:13:37,490
Now you may say, why is that good?

228
00:13:38,170 --> 00:13:40,350
Well, mending absorbs a lot of experience.

229
00:13:41,730 --> 00:13:46,570
So by using this pickaxe, I can get to 33 way faster.

230
00:13:50,660 --> 00:13:51,660
What do I have in here?

231
00:13:54,360 --> 00:13:55,200
Ent rods.

232
00:13:55,640 --> 00:13:55,780
Right.

233
00:14:00,120 --> 00:14:00,620
Jump.

234
00:14:01,380 --> 00:14:02,880
I should have actually just gone up.

235
00:14:03,240 --> 00:14:03,340
Yeah.

236
00:14:04,500 --> 00:14:05,140
I'm gonna go up here.

237
00:14:06,420 --> 00:14:10,340
Or even better, I am going to... Shit.

238
00:14:22,320 --> 00:14:23,420
Gonna make a ladder here.

239
00:14:23,800 --> 00:14:26,780
Because I will be going up and down this in the future, I just know it.

240
00:14:31,720 --> 00:14:32,720
One diorite.

241
00:14:38,020 --> 00:14:38,480
There.

242
00:14:40,100 --> 00:14:41,160
Make this as well.

243
00:14:42,660 --> 00:14:43,540
Look at that!

244
00:14:44,500 --> 00:14:44,960
Beautiful.

245
00:14:52,440 --> 00:14:53,460
Ah, fuck.

246
00:14:53,720 --> 00:14:53,820
Wait.

247
00:14:56,220 --> 00:14:58,060
We gotta do this instead.

248
00:14:59,460 --> 00:15:00,220
There we go.

249
00:15:00,540 --> 00:15:02,220
A little janky, but it works.

250
00:15:04,760 --> 00:15:06,020
Oh, I'm mega close.

251
00:15:06,240 --> 00:15:06,620
Wait, what?

252
00:15:06,860 --> 00:15:07,660
Where am I right now?

253
00:15:08,940 --> 00:15:10,280
The surface is right here.

254
00:15:12,760 --> 00:15:13,280
Oh.

255
00:15:14,100 --> 00:15:14,900
Oh, no.

256
00:15:16,520 --> 00:15:17,480
It's this again.

257
00:15:18,820 --> 00:15:19,960
Maybe it's time...

258
00:15:20,160 --> 00:15:21,940
To get to the bottom of what's going on here.

259
00:15:24,780 --> 00:15:27,280
I hear it... this direction.

260
00:15:36,480 --> 00:15:38,540
I am actually right underneath my village.

261
00:15:39,420 --> 00:15:40,880
I'm actually happy to hear that.

262
00:15:42,800 --> 00:15:46,000
Because that means the places I just lit were very important.

263
00:16:05,490 --> 00:16:08,370
As soon as I hear him behind me, I'll turn around.

264
00:16:18,890 --> 00:16:19,370
Okay.

265
00:16:27,150 --> 00:16:33,310
Where the... Now it's stopped.

266
00:16:42,210 --> 00:16:43,450
What the fuck?

267
00:16:45,850 --> 00:16:53,790
So it's somewhere... Do we have, like, a place where the water is flowing into a little cave with water inside?

268
00:16:59,030 --> 00:17:00,410
Okay, so there's nothing here.

269
00:17:10,120 --> 00:17:11,060
Make a sound.

