494
00:30:44,100 --> 00:30:45,040
What have I been doing?

495
00:30:47,460 --> 00:30:48,420
Oh yeah, look at all this.

496
00:30:51,900 --> 00:30:52,840
That is wonderful.

497
00:30:53,260 --> 00:30:53,720
What is it?

498
00:30:53,920 --> 00:30:55,660
I feel like some of these are just drying out.

499
00:30:56,660 --> 00:30:58,640
Maybe it's like a random chance for that to dry out.

500
00:30:59,680 --> 00:31:00,960
I need my hoe for that.

501
00:31:03,610 --> 00:31:06,030
Yeah, let's take the golden one, why not?

502
00:31:06,990 --> 00:31:11,250
A golden hole... for golden times.

503
00:31:12,250 --> 00:31:15,830
And now... seats...

504
00:31:24,350 --> 00:31:27,150
I'm tempted to go over there with some bone meal immediately, but I'm not gonna.

505
00:31:29,130 --> 00:31:29,770
Not gonna.

506
00:31:31,610 --> 00:31:32,010
Leather.

507
00:31:33,010 --> 00:31:34,130
Look how much leather I have.

508
00:31:34,770 --> 00:31:35,850
I'm rich in leather.

509
00:31:37,390 --> 00:31:38,510
Cook more steaks.

510
00:31:43,370 --> 00:31:45,450
Okay, so we're at 11 now.

511
00:31:45,670 --> 00:31:48,890
It wouldn't surprise me if the number is eight.

512
00:31:49,690 --> 00:31:52,270
Eight coals for one stack of cobblestone.

513
00:31:52,710 --> 00:31:54,010
I can see that happening.

514
00:31:56,050 --> 00:31:58,630
Let's pay attention to when that is done.

515
00:32:00,470 --> 00:32:01,030
Okay.

516
00:32:03,410 --> 00:32:06,350
Should I... I'm not gonna check the Orphan Crusher.

517
00:32:07,050 --> 00:32:08,710
Once again, we're gonna wait till the end.

518
00:32:10,050 --> 00:32:11,210
Also gonna get rid of my hole.

519
00:32:14,640 --> 00:32:16,860
Now, I have three Elytras, baby!

520
00:32:17,100 --> 00:32:17,840
Look at that!

521
00:32:18,840 --> 00:32:21,600
But of course, we need mending.

522
00:32:22,020 --> 00:32:27,120
So we gotta go back into the mines and find the guy I know about.

523
00:32:27,780 --> 00:32:28,920
Because I know a guy.

524
00:32:29,220 --> 00:32:30,320
And he's down there.

525
00:32:32,560 --> 00:32:33,800
He's like a recluse.

526
00:32:33,920 --> 00:32:38,060
He's like the genius hermit who knows the mending enchant.

527
00:32:39,180 --> 00:32:40,620
And we're gonna get it from him.

528
00:32:42,540 --> 00:32:44,800
So let's just remember what we need for that.

529
00:32:45,880 --> 00:32:52,580
I do believe for something like that he would need a book and money, right?

530
00:32:52,940 --> 00:32:53,940
Books and money.

531
00:32:57,420 --> 00:33:01,580
Let's... I forgot how many books... I think just one, but let's take like three just in case.

532
00:33:01,580 --> 00:33:02,600
I'm not quite sure.

533
00:33:03,780 --> 00:33:04,580
Put them in there.

534
00:33:05,000 --> 00:33:05,980
And we need money.

535
00:33:10,180 --> 00:33:12,280
Take a full stack, because I'm not sure.

536
00:33:13,880 --> 00:33:15,520
To be completely honest with you.

537
00:33:17,080 --> 00:33:21,560
Now, the shield could use a slight upgrade.

538
00:33:22,540 --> 00:33:28,180
See, shields like this that are half broken, I kind of just want to throw them in the lava.

539
00:33:28,900 --> 00:33:30,860
Because repairing them is nonsensical.

540
00:33:32,140 --> 00:33:33,500
When you can just make a new one.

541
