1089
01:09:31,960 --> 01:09:33,220
Diamonds... Sticks?

1090
01:09:33,300 --> 01:09:33,960
I don't have sticks.

1091
01:09:34,140 --> 01:09:34,280
Fuck.

1092
01:09:41,870 --> 01:09:43,630
Uh, pickaxe.

1093
01:09:43,630 --> 01:09:44,670
There we go.

1094
01:09:55,670 --> 01:09:56,610
Oh no, not that one.

1095
01:09:56,810 --> 01:09:57,090
This one.

1096
01:09:57,770 --> 01:09:58,830
Yeah, look, 33.

1097
01:10:00,850 --> 01:10:03,790
I could do that right now and get a pretty sick pickaxe.

1098
01:10:03,790 --> 01:10:05,590
Although it is... Ah, man, that is expensive, though.

1099
01:10:06,210 --> 01:10:06,590
You know what?

1100
01:10:06,630 --> 01:10:10,450
Before I do anything, let's just go to the enchanting table and see what options I have.

1101
01:10:10,630 --> 01:10:10,950
Who knows?

1102
01:10:11,090 --> 01:10:12,150
Maybe there's something insane here.

1103
01:10:13,830 --> 01:10:15,810
Let's just try everything before we go nuts.

1104
01:10:19,170 --> 01:10:20,310
Uh, get one book.

1105
01:10:24,010 --> 01:10:25,230
I don't need to put this in, actually.

1106
01:10:25,310 --> 01:10:25,770
I can just check.

1107
01:10:27,350 --> 01:10:28,850
Loyalty impaling.

1108
01:10:32,550 --> 01:10:32,950
Impaling.

1109
01:10:36,110 --> 01:10:36,810
The hell?

1110
01:10:41,390 --> 01:10:42,250
Silk touch?

1111
01:10:42,690 --> 01:10:42,910
Yo!

1112
01:10:43,710 --> 01:10:45,510
I actually need that.

1113
01:10:46,590 --> 01:10:47,110
Hmm.

1114
01:10:48,550 --> 01:10:50,270
See, now I'm conflicted.

1115
01:10:51,270 --> 01:10:53,170
I feel like I should do this instead.

1116
01:10:54,670 --> 01:10:57,990
And then maybe repair the pickaxe in a different way.

1117
01:11:01,570 --> 01:11:04,610
Uh... Hmm.

1118
01:11:05,450 --> 01:11:05,790
Oh, right.

1119
01:11:05,870 --> 01:11:06,670
This one cannot be done.

1120
01:11:06,870 --> 01:11:08,550
So this is... Ah, three lapis.

1121
01:11:11,540 --> 01:11:13,060
I think I'll do it.

1122
01:11:23,160 --> 01:11:24,240
Easy.

1123
01:11:24,780 --> 01:11:26,180
Easy money.

1124
01:11:27,720 --> 01:11:28,800
Unbelievable.

1125
01:11:35,120 --> 01:11:36,820
Not bad either, is it?

1126
01:11:37,640 --> 01:11:39,020
Put mending on that, maybe?

1127
01:11:39,700 --> 01:11:40,760
It's only four.

1128
01:11:41,300 --> 01:11:44,160
Ah, but wait, let's not do that now, because we're still level 31.

1129
01:11:44,900 --> 01:11:47,060
Let's check what other options we have here first.

1130
01:11:49,120 --> 01:11:49,940
Quick charge.

1131
01:11:50,180 --> 01:11:50,460
Boo!

1132
01:11:51,380 --> 01:11:52,220
Nobody likes that.

1133
01:11:53,900 --> 01:11:54,740
Unbreaking three.

1134
01:11:58,730 --> 01:12:00,490
Well, I mean, hmm.

1135
01:12:02,950 --> 01:12:08,390
Silk Touch is nice, but I kind of hate having it on the pickaxe.

1136
01:12:08,630 --> 01:12:17,430
This is only for picking up very certain blocks like stone and, well, also the ender chest.

1137
01:12:19,430 --> 01:12:22,670
Other than that, it's kind of annoying, you know?

1138
01:12:25,470 --> 01:12:27,530
Because not everything I want to pick up and take with me.

1139
01:12:27,670 --> 01:12:29,190
Some of it I want to pick up and leave.

1140
01:12:33,820 --> 01:12:35,940
What about this flame?

1141
01:12:38,800 --> 01:12:40,620
Oh, right, I can't do it to that one.

1142
01:12:41,580 --> 01:12:42,940
Well, well, well.

1143
01:12:46,040 --> 01:12:48,200
Maybe I'll just try another pickaxe.

1144
01:12:48,320 --> 01:12:49,060
Is that crazy?

1145
01:12:50,400 --> 01:12:53,440
Because Unbreaking 3 is, I think, the highest.

1146
01:12:54,760 --> 01:12:56,000
It's not a bad idea.

1147
01:12:59,220 --> 01:13:02,220
There's a possibility we get something nuts out of this too, right?

1148
01:13:16,030 --> 01:13:16,990
Easy game.

1149
01:13:19,990 --> 01:13:21,590
Exactly what I needed.

1150
01:13:23,390 --> 01:13:24,390
Thank you.

1151
01:13:25,310 --> 01:13:28,750
And then, on this guy, we're gonna put mending now.

1152
01:13:29,030 --> 01:13:29,970
Because we have it.

1153
01:13:34,680 --> 01:13:36,000
So we go like this.

1154
01:13:38,240 --> 01:13:38,980
Like that.

1155
01:13:40,100 --> 01:13:41,680
Oh yeah, baby.

1156
01:13:43,680 --> 01:13:44,160
Wonderful!

1157
01:13:45,420 --> 01:13:48,040
Now we have... Oh my god, this is actually perfect.

1158
01:13:48,380 --> 01:13:51,360
Am I glad I didn't choose to repair this one?

1159
01:13:52,580 --> 01:13:59,140
I kind of want to throw this in the fire as a symbolic gesture to put a nail in the coffin and say, that sucks.

1160
01:14:00,400 --> 01:14:01,340
Don't want that.

1161
01:14:05,140 --> 01:14:08,000
I'm actually so tired of this pickaxe, it has brought me so much misery.

1162
01:14:10,700 --> 01:14:14,160
Ah, before we do that... I'm gonna go disenchant it.

1163
01:14:16,260 --> 01:14:18,180
Shitty pickaxe.

1164
01:14:20,060 --> 01:14:20,540
Yeah!

1165
01:14:21,400 --> 01:14:22,760
How you like them apples?

1166
01:14:23,280 --> 01:14:24,340
And you know what else?

1167
01:14:25,100 --> 01:14:25,820
Fuck you.

1168
01:14:26,500 --> 01:14:26,900
Boom!

1169
01:14:27,380 --> 01:14:27,860
Gone.

1170
01:14:29,200 --> 01:14:30,380
Man, that was satisfying.

1171
01:14:30,640 --> 01:14:31,580
That actually felt amazing.

1172
01:14:32,780 --> 01:14:33,620
Out with you.

1173
01:14:33,840 --> 01:14:34,640
And then we have this guy.

1174
01:14:34,860 --> 01:14:35,720
Ooh, you know what?

1175
01:14:39,880 --> 01:14:42,660
Uh, efficiency for... Oh, yeah.

1176
01:14:44,920 --> 01:14:45,620
Good night!

1177
01:14:46,940 --> 01:14:48,160
Shitty pickaxe.

1178
01:14:51,970 --> 01:14:52,790
Boom!

1179
01:14:53,310 --> 01:14:55,590
Oh, I feel cleansed.

1180
01:14:55,810 --> 01:14:57,210
My soul is whole.

1181
01:14:59,030 --> 01:15:00,850
Away, away.

1182
01:15:02,010 --> 01:15:03,130
Very nice.

1183
01:15:03,410 --> 01:15:06,190
Now we gotta put mending on Ilytra.

1184
01:15:09,760 --> 01:15:10,760
Do it right now.

1185
01:15:13,580 --> 01:15:14,060
Boom.

1186
01:15:14,980 --> 01:15:15,460
Fixed.

1187
01:15:17,320 --> 01:15:18,120
Very nice.

1188
01:15:20,220 --> 01:15:20,960
Done that.

1189
01:15:22,520 --> 01:15:24,920
You know what, let's just put a mending on another one.

1190
01:15:25,860 --> 01:15:26,800
Why not, right?

1191
01:15:28,020 --> 01:15:31,260
I will probably lose this Elytra at some point, so having a backup?

1192
01:15:31,420 --> 01:15:32,440
Hey, pretty good.

1193
01:15:33,160 --> 01:15:33,460
Yeah.

1194
01:15:34,220 --> 01:15:35,180
Not bad at all.

1195
01:15:36,540 --> 01:15:37,020
Boom.

1196
01:15:39,830 --> 01:15:40,770
Boom, boom, boom.

1197
01:15:41,010 --> 01:15:42,350
I want you in my room.

1198
01:15:46,410 --> 01:15:47,630
Okay, very good.

1199
01:15:49,050 --> 01:15:52,330
And then... We got pluralis.

1200
01:15:52,430 --> 01:15:53,410
I don't really need that right now.

1201
01:15:53,570 --> 01:15:54,130
Put this in here.

1202
01:15:55,750 --> 01:15:56,730
And bones.

1203
01:15:56,970 --> 01:15:58,010
How many bones do I have?

1204
01:15:59,650 --> 01:16:01,370
I just need ten.

1205
01:16:02,650 --> 01:16:03,550
Rest goes in here.

1206
01:16:05,720 --> 01:16:06,540
In you go.

1207
01:16:06,720 --> 01:16:08,300
Look at these amazing pig axes.

1208
01:16:08,800 --> 01:16:09,520
Fuck yeah.

1209
01:16:09,740 --> 01:16:16,020
Oh, it's gonna be such a beautiful experience going back down into the mines now and feeling the difference.

1210
01:16:16,980 --> 01:16:18,340
Oh, can't wait.

1211
01:16:23,610 --> 01:16:24,510
Steaks for me?

1212
01:16:26,450 --> 01:16:27,850
How's the harvest coming along?

1213
01:16:28,630 --> 01:16:32,170
Honestly, I'm gonna go over there and just give it a quick rub.

1214
01:16:33,470 --> 01:16:34,910
You know, quick rub.

1215
01:16:42,170 --> 01:16:43,170
There we go.

1216
01:16:43,330 --> 01:16:44,310
Wrap that up.

1217
01:16:44,770 --> 01:16:46,010
Wrap, wrap, wrap, wrap, wrap, wrap.

1218
01:16:48,110 --> 01:16:49,330
Wrap the wheat, people.

1219
01:16:49,890 --> 01:16:52,290
You gotta wrap the wheat and eat the lettuce.

1220
01:16:53,150 --> 01:16:54,730
You gotta eat the lettuce.

1221
01:16:56,290 --> 01:16:56,770
Okay.

1222
01:16:58,470 --> 01:16:59,890
Now we go feeding.

1223
01:17:00,650 --> 01:17:02,350
So that we can do some breeding.

1224
01:17:04,630 --> 01:17:05,110
Seats.

1225
01:17:06,470 --> 01:17:07,510
Nothing has dried out.

1226
01:17:07,630 --> 01:17:08,050
Wonderful.

1227
01:17:10,360 --> 01:17:12,620
Everything is nice and wet.

1228
01:17:13,280 --> 01:17:15,360
Why is it all sounding so wrong right now?

1229
01:17:15,980 --> 01:17:19,880
I'm not even intending it to be... maybe a little bit, but not to this extent.

1230
01:17:21,880 --> 01:17:22,780
No, I need this.

1231
01:17:23,360 --> 01:17:24,280
All right, eating time!

1232
01:17:27,690 --> 01:17:28,430
Here you go.

1233
01:17:29,030 --> 01:17:29,790
Everyone eats.

1234
01:17:31,230 --> 01:17:32,350
Man, it's so satisfying.

1235
01:17:33,350 --> 01:17:34,810
Kind of what makes me... Oh!

1236
01:17:35,630 --> 01:17:36,670
Oh-ho-ho!

1237
01:17:37,010 --> 01:17:38,550
You tried to get out there, didn't ya?

1238
01:17:39,670 --> 01:17:40,290
Who what?

1239
01:17:40,350 --> 01:17:40,870
What was your name?

1240
01:17:41,330 --> 01:17:42,090
Who was it?

1241
01:17:43,530 --> 01:17:44,930
I will have you for dinner.

1242
01:17:46,050 --> 01:17:47,870
I'll have all of you for dinner, actually.

1243
01:17:49,930 --> 01:17:53,230
In time... It'll happen.

1244
01:17:53,690 --> 01:17:55,390
Now, the wheat goes back in the wheat box.

1245
01:18:00,250 --> 01:18:01,210
That looks so good.

1246
01:18:01,310 --> 01:18:01,770
I love that house.

1247
01:18:02,610 --> 01:18:03,510
I'm happy with it.

1248
01:18:04,230 --> 01:18:04,550
So happy.

1249
01:18:04,710 --> 01:18:06,130
Book goes back in the book box.

1250
01:18:06,630 --> 01:18:07,810
Also called a bookshelf.

1251
01:18:08,050 --> 01:18:09,370
But it's not actually a shelf, it's a box.

1252
01:18:09,510 --> 01:18:10,050
So I was right.

1253
01:18:12,350 --> 01:18:12,790
Tortures.

1254
01:18:13,670 --> 01:18:14,510
Baked taters.

1255
01:18:17,050 --> 01:18:17,750
Fuck yeah.

1256
01:18:18,110 --> 01:18:19,510
We got the pickaxes back.

1257
01:18:20,750 --> 01:18:21,790
Lapis lazuli.

1258
01:18:23,350 --> 01:18:24,410
And bone meal.

1259
01:18:24,950 --> 01:18:25,890
Also got some gold.

1260
01:18:26,370 --> 01:18:27,250
We can cook that.

1261
01:18:29,980 --> 01:18:30,880
In you go.

1262
01:18:31,820 --> 01:18:32,820
Do I have more gold?

1263
01:18:33,840 --> 01:18:35,440
Didn't I find way more than this?

1264
01:18:35,580 --> 01:18:36,300
Am I crazy?

1265
01:18:38,060 --> 01:18:40,460
I feel like I found way more than that, but okay.

1266
01:18:43,700 --> 01:18:44,440
Hey, Kaos.

1267
01:18:46,580 --> 01:18:48,600
A song for you and your people.

1268
01:18:51,310 --> 01:18:53,170
How do you like them apples?

1269
01:18:54,450 --> 01:18:55,090
Eat it.

1270
01:18:57,770 --> 01:19:00,310
Um... Oh, right, I have gold here.

1271
01:19:00,550 --> 01:19:01,430
That explains it.

1272
01:19:06,490 --> 01:19:07,270
Good stuff.

1273
01:19:12,510 --> 01:19:13,610
Where did I get sugar?

1274
01:19:14,670 --> 01:19:16,990
Did I get that from the guy with the potion?

1275
01:19:19,190 --> 01:19:20,690
Spider eye is a drop?

1276
01:19:26,300 --> 01:19:27,440
Go and... there.

1277
01:19:27,880 --> 01:19:28,820
Ah, but I cooked this.

1278
01:19:30,340 --> 01:19:31,260
There we are.

1279
01:19:32,380 --> 01:19:32,900
Okay.

1280
01:19:35,640 --> 01:19:38,000
Let's... enchant maybe a little bit more.

1281
01:19:38,380 --> 01:19:39,860
Since I'm still level 21.

1282
01:19:40,140 --> 01:19:40,300
Mmm.

1283
01:19:40,580 --> 01:19:44,120
Don't really know what to enchant, but... Can I maybe repair something?

1284
01:19:45,180 --> 01:19:46,980
Maybe these boots or this helmet.

1285
01:19:49,580 --> 01:19:50,480
Yeah, why not?

1286
01:19:50,700 --> 01:19:52,040
We have so many diamonds anyway.

1287
01:19:53,500 --> 01:19:58,360
Let's make new boots, and pants, and just prepare them.

1288
01:20:06,680 --> 01:20:07,980
Oh no!

1289
01:20:09,000 --> 01:20:09,760
Fuck!

1290
01:20:11,800 --> 01:20:13,040
I need iron.

1291
01:20:15,620 --> 01:20:17,420
Uh, anvil?

1292
01:20:20,560 --> 01:20:21,520
Also, where are you?

1293
01:20:21,620 --> 01:20:22,020
I heard you.

1294
01:20:23,900 --> 01:20:25,260
Are you getting inside somehow?

1295
01:20:25,600 --> 01:20:26,500
There's no way, right?

1296
01:20:27,900 --> 01:20:29,340
Not with my new improved wall.

1297
01:20:29,560 --> 01:20:29,920
Oh, wait a minute.

1298
01:20:30,020 --> 01:20:30,980
It's kind of dark here.

1299
01:20:32,340 --> 01:20:33,240
We have no lights?

1300
01:20:35,360 --> 01:20:36,140
Oh my god.

1301
01:20:36,240 --> 01:20:37,760
All the lights I had on the wall are gone.

1302
01:20:39,620 --> 01:20:40,960
I did not think about this.

1303
01:20:43,600 --> 01:20:44,640
That's kind of a problem.

1304
01:20:48,580 --> 01:20:49,960
Am I seeing any enemies?

1305
01:20:51,100 --> 01:20:51,620
No.

1306
01:20:58,640 --> 01:20:59,340
Got him.

1307
01:21:00,060 --> 01:21:02,760
The wild beast has been taken care of.

1308
01:21:03,900 --> 01:21:05,420
That's a bit too dark over here.

1309
01:21:11,200 --> 01:21:12,280
What's that doing there?

1310
01:21:19,410 --> 01:21:20,150
What is that?

1311
01:21:20,810 --> 01:21:21,990
Oh, it's music!

1312
01:21:22,170 --> 01:21:29,310
I thought... I thought this thing was making it... You know, like... I don't even know how to explain what I just thought.

1313
01:21:29,590 --> 01:21:36,470
Like, it was reverberating at a certain frequency, producing a sound wave that was constant in... I don't even know.

1314
01:21:36,590 --> 01:21:36,990
I don't know.

1315
01:21:37,310 --> 01:21:37,990
Holy shit.

1316
01:21:39,550 --> 01:21:40,030
Anvil.

1317
01:21:42,310 --> 01:21:43,030
Anvil time.

1318
01:21:46,450 --> 01:21:48,210
There, there, boom.

1319
01:21:48,810 --> 01:21:49,290
Repaired.

1320
01:21:50,190 --> 01:21:51,270
We are so back.

1321
01:21:51,830 --> 01:21:53,450
In fact, we've been back for a while now.

1322
01:21:55,250 --> 01:22:03,610
The only problem with having elytra is that it's not just very good protection, but... I also don't want to carry around a breastplate at all times.

1323
01:22:04,790 --> 01:22:06,450
Maybe I do want to carry it around.

1324
01:22:07,910 --> 01:22:08,590
Not sure.

1325
01:22:09,270 --> 01:22:10,590
We're gonna have to see about that.

1326
01:22:11,950 --> 01:22:13,130
Leather and mining.

1327
01:22:13,270 --> 01:22:13,570
Put it in.

1328
01:22:16,650 --> 01:22:16,950
Okay.

1329
01:22:16,950 --> 01:22:18,670
Now we go to bed, and then we go to the nether.

1330
01:22:20,270 --> 01:22:20,790
Oh, yes.

1331
01:22:20,870 --> 01:22:21,470
You heard me right.

1332
01:22:22,150 --> 01:22:24,030
In fact... Yeah, good.

1333
01:22:24,290 --> 01:22:24,630
Good, good, good.

1334
01:22:25,630 --> 01:22:26,790
Bed... Bedtime!

1335
01:22:32,870 --> 01:22:33,390
Oh, yeah.

1336
01:22:37,040 --> 01:22:37,480
Jaxter!

1337
01:22:38,040 --> 01:22:40,660
Oh, oh, dude, there's something I want to try!

1338
01:22:43,020 --> 01:22:45,060
Ever since I made that experiment in the end.

1339
01:22:47,740 --> 01:22:49,800
Torch... I don't think I need more torches for this.

1340
01:22:56,680 --> 01:22:57,560
Give me some beds.

1341
01:22:58,920 --> 01:23:00,120
A black bed, why not?

1342
01:23:03,080 --> 01:23:08,380
Also... Where's my... TNT?

1343
01:23:10,600 --> 01:23:11,540
It's not even here.

1344
01:23:11,960 --> 01:23:14,000
Where the hell is my... Ah, there we go.

1345
01:23:15,300 --> 01:23:20,820
Now, I know this works with redstone, but we may not need it if we have protection like we did in the end.

1346
01:23:22,360 --> 01:23:23,980
So, we're gonna need...

1347
01:23:24,140 --> 01:23:27,460
Something like... this.

1348
01:23:28,340 --> 01:23:29,020
A lot.

1349
01:23:29,140 --> 01:23:31,160
Maybe not actually, I'm gonna get a lot just for mining.

1350
01:23:31,660 --> 01:23:32,200
Yeah, put it back.

1351
01:23:33,540 --> 01:23:36,280
Goathorn, I think it's not necessary right now.

1352
01:23:37,400 --> 01:23:40,780
Yeah, I may actually just leave that at home for now, even though it pains me.

1353
01:23:42,800 --> 01:23:47,240
Silk touch, I think I'll bring that as well, and then bring a ender chest.

1354
01:23:47,820 --> 01:23:48,840
Oh, the maze!

1355
01:23:48,880 --> 01:23:49,840
Let's bring that, of course.

1356
01:23:51,490 --> 01:23:52,790
Then again, this one has looting.

1357
01:23:53,670 --> 01:23:55,210
Can I put looting on a mace?

1358
01:23:56,590 --> 01:23:57,630
I'm not quite sure.

